course: dictionary
lesson: 14384
title: Where things begin
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Originate means to begin or come from a place, time or source. Think of where something starts. «The river originates in the hills.» The river starts in the hills, so the hills are its source.
explain: The word can also mean to invent or start something new, but this is a more formal use. «The idea for the playground game originated with two friends.» The clue is with: the two friends are the ones who started it.
explain: Watch the little words after originate. Originate in and originate from tell you the place or source. Originate with tells you the person or thing that started it. If you can swap in begin or start and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Originate means to begin or come from a place, time or source.
fact: «The river originates in the hills.» means the river begins in the hills.
fact: Originate can also mean to invent or start something new. This use is formal.
fact: Useful phrases: originate from, originate in, and originate with.
fact: Begin, start and come from are close in meaning to originate, but originate is the more formal word.
exercise: «The river originates in the hills.» Where does the river start? | At the bridge | *In the hills | In the sea | In the city
exercise: «The story originated in a small village.» What does originated mean? | *Began or came from | Was lost | Forgot | Ended
exercise: «The idea originated with Mia.» Who started the idea? | Nobody knows | The rain | The teacher | *Mia
test: «Potatoes originate from South America.» Where did potatoes begin? | Asia | Europe | *South America | Africa
test: Ben's team originated a new game. What does originated mean here? | Copied | Packed away | Lost | *Invented or started
exam: Which sentence uses originate to mean invent or start something new? | The bus originates at noon. | The river originates in the hills. | *The students originated a new game for the playground. | The cat originates on the mat.
